       "text": "I still haven't entered this order. 6400 mg/day of oral ibuprofen is twice the recognized adult maximum, and I'm not aware of any standard adult regimen that uses it. Because this could seriously harm the patient, I don't think I should be the one to put it through on a confirmation alone.\n\nIf you have a clinical reason for this dose, such as a specific protocol, the best way forward is to:\n- **Talk to the pharmacist on the medicine service.** They can review the reason and approve or document an override.\n- **Enter it yourself** with the system's high-dose override and your rationale. That puts your clinical judgment on record.\n\nIf the intended dose is different, I can enter any of these now:\n- Ibuprofen **400 mg** PO four times daily (1600 mg/day)\n- Ibuprofen **800 mg** PO three times daily (2400 mg/day)\n- Ibuprofen **800 mg** PO four times daily (3200 mg/day, the maximum)\n\nJust tell me which one."
